   "text": "I'll search for documented reports of this NumPy compatibility error.\nI found matching error reports \u2014 now I'll open the sources to verify them.\nKnown issue: pyarrow 26 requires NumPy 2 at import but its wheel declares no NumPy runtime dependency, so resolvers can keep NumPy 1.26.4 alongside pyarrow 26 via `datasets` and fail at import. Same failure documented as `pyarrow requires NumPy 2.0 or newer` breaking use with pinned `numpy==1.26.4`.\n\n{\"status\": \"found\", \"sources\": [{\"url\": \"https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5372\", \"title\": \"[CI] Preserve NumPy 1.x support by constraining PyArrow\", \"why\": \"Describes pyarrow 26 requiring NumPy 2 while retaining NumPy 1.26.4 via datasets, causing import failure\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/commit/151bc09e17e319b6d2ddb0b8cb397826362ed118\", \"title\": \"Fix numpy/pyarrow conflict in the XPU Docker image (#49582)\", \"why\": \"Documents pyarrow>=26.0.0 raising 'pyarrow requires NumPy 2.0 or newer' when numpy is held at 1.26.4\"}]}"
